  "summary": "EFF announced it is representing DeFlock.me creator Will Freeman in rejecting a cease-and-desist letter from Flock Safety, which claimed the anti-ALPR mapping project dilutes its trademark. EFF argues the project is protected noncommercial criticism under the First Amendment and federal anti-dilution carve-outs.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The company sent DeFlock.me and its creator Will Freeman a cease-and-desist letter, claiming that the project dilutes its trademark.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Federal anti-dilution law includes express carve-outs for any noncommercial use of a mark and for any use in connection with criticizing or commenting on the mark owner or its products.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "DeFlock has mapped out more than 16,000 individual camera locations, more than a third of which are Flock Safety devices.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    }
